Drop the reveal animation on "Show more" items

Items appended by "Show more" no longer carry the .reveal class. The scroll
fade exists for content that arrives because you scrolled to it; these arrive
because you clicked, with the section already in view, so the animation reads
as lag on an explicit action — worsened by the 80ms stagger fading a batch in
one after another. The initially visible items keep .reveal, since those do
arrive by scrolling, and the heading is untouched.

With no .reveal nodes mounted on expand, the observer has nothing to do, so
`expanded` is removed from the dependency array again. The comment records that
re-adding .reveal to expanded items requires re-adding `expanded`, otherwise
this regresses into the "show more does nothing" bug fixed one commit earlier.

Verified by timing rather than appearance: computed opacity sampled at +0ms,
+60ms and +560ms after the click. Appended items read opacity 1 at +0ms
(previously 0, fading over ~240ms) with reveal false, while the first two keep
reveal true. 13/13 unit, typecheck, eslint incl. components/lib, static build,
158/158 QA, 33/33 motion, 21/21 overflow.
